{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"conclusive-daemonic-graywolf","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\n\n`bedrock-spend-cap` can enforce on a spend figure that includes static seed rates or `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K`, but the handler has no provenance flag telling consumers that the figure is partly estimated. That capability was cut from `3083-ada3` so the empirical-rate fix can stay focused.\n\n## Current code facts\n\n`_rate_for()` at `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py:226-274` returns a bare `float`. Its paths are empirical match at lines 261-263, seed at lines 265-267, input-derived empirical rate at lines 269-271, and fail-closed fallback at lines 273-274. The caller cannot distinguish those sources.\n\n`_metered_spend()` at `handler.py:280-341` accumulates `total += units_1k * _rate_for(model_id, metric_name, rates)` at line 337 and returns only the numeric total at line 341. There is no accumulator for source provenance.\n\nThe handler saves state through `_save_state(state)` at `handler.py:143-144` and calls it at line 589. The return payload at `handler.py:590-600` includes dollar values and source status, but no estimated-rate field. WARNING notification text is built at `handler.py:550-559`; TRIP notification text is built at `handler.py:578-587`. Neither message identifies seed or fallback participation.\n\n## Required change\n\nChange `_rate_for()`'s return contract so callers receive both the numeric rate and a bounded source value such as `empirical`, `seed`, `empirical_scaled`, or `fallback`. Update every caller in this handler in the same patch.\n\nChange `_metered_spend()` to accumulate both the numeric spend total and whether any component used `seed` or `fallback`. Preserve the existing numeric behavior for empirical and empirical-scaled rates.\n\nThread the provenance through the handler response payload, the saved SSM state dict, and the WARNING and TRIP `_notify` call sites. Use one field name consistently; `metered_estimated` is acceptable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_rate_for()` returns the numeric rate and a bounded source value.\n- [ ] `_rate_for()` labels exact empirical matches as `empirical`.\n- [ ] `_rate_for()` labels seed matches as `seed`.\n- [ ] `_rate_for()` labels input-derived empirical matches as `empirical_scaled`.\n- [ ] `_rate_for()` labels `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K` fallback matches as `fallback`.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend()` accumulates the existing numeric spend total.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend()` reports estimated provenance when any component source is `seed`.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend()` reports estimated provenance when any component source is `fallback`.\n- [ ] The handler return payload includes `metered_estimated: true` when metered spend includes a seed rate.\n- [ ] The handler return payload includes `metered_estimated: true` when metered spend includes `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K`.\n- [ ] The saved SSM state includes `metered_estimated: true` after a run whose metered spend includes a seed rate.\n- [ ] The saved SSM state includes `metered_estimated: true` after a run whose metered spend includes `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K`.\n- [ ] WARNING SNS text includes `estimated` when warning spend includes a seed rate.\n- [ ] TRIP SNS text includes `estimated` when trip spend includes `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k estimated` exits 0.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Testing\n\nDuring development run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k estimated`. Before push run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`. Before Gerrit push run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nDo not change the Claude Marketplace CE service filter in this ticket; `3083-ada3` owns that empirical-rate and authoritative-spend fix.","id":"d082-5fe8-0f98-49fc","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bedrock spend cap does not expose seed or fallback rate provenance"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789878721360521519,"uuid":"035324a3-d3a8-423a-9368-f3451acb9c1b"}